  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "CpefXyLGMO+zTsyD6uiBYPAFciA=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:48:57.447Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The v6.0.0 notes describe the reactor's write model and sync pipeline as a **complete rewrite**, and the reliability changes are the substance:\n\n- **per-document quarantine** \u2014 a failing document is isolated *instead of blocking the entire remote*;\n- a **persistent dead-letter store**;\n- **buffered batched mailboxes** and abort signals on GQL channels;\n- **cursor-based paging** for large sync batches, with `getOperations` now paging **across scopes**;\n- **`DocumentIntegrityService`** \u2014 validates and rebuilds document keyframes and snapshots;\n- **job timeout** via abort signals propagated through the whole job pipeline;\n- **yield utilities** for cooperative scheduling in the job executor;\n- **exponential backoff with jitter** on retries;\n- a **`test-sync-queue` CLI app** for detecting sync drift on large drives, plus `profiling/reactor-direct.ts --docs 1000 --otel` for direct reactor performance testing.\n\nBug fixes from the same release that describe current behaviour: orphan reshuffle and cross-batch FIFO bugs fixed, documents with out-of-order `ADD_RELATIONSHIP` now correctly backfilled, deleted documents no longer returned by queries and jobs targeting them not retried, and the GQL channel handling abort signals, backpressure and dead-letter placement correctly.\n\nTwo of these are load-bearing for anything built on sync today: quarantine is why one bad document does not stall a drive, and the integrity service is why a corrupted keyframe is repairable rather than terminal.\n\n## Provenance\n- `apps/academy/docs/academy/ReleaseNotes/index.md` \u2014 v6.0.0 \u203a New Features \u203a Reactor \u2014 Rewritten Write Model & Sync Engine; Bug Fixes\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:48:57.447Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:48:57.447Z"
    }
  },
